/*
 * MiniRocket Fused CONV+PPV — Network AXI-Stream wrapper (buffer-then-classify)
 *
 * Structural sibling of fpga-network/minirocket_dpr/src/minirocket.cpp (same
 * AXIS-in/AXIS-out + m_axi model-param top shape, same Bug-B output sideband,
 * same #if BUILD==1 free-run gate), but the compute core is swapped from
 * DP-Reuse (incremental, classify-every-packet) to the Fused CONV+PPV
 * full-recompute core from minirocket_modular/_recovered_src_b2b4089
 * (feature_extraction_v16_fixed.cpp + scaler.cpp + classifier.cpp), collapsed
 * from 3 separate AXI-stream kernels into one top, called inline like
 * minirocket_dpr does conv -> scaler -> classifier.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * v4 (2026-07-06) -- TRUE on-chip free-run + packed emit, combining THREE
 * previously separately-validated pieces:
 *
 *   1. v2's `#pragma HLS DATAFLOW` producer/consumer decouple (this file's
 *      structure below, preserved verbatim from
 *      minirocket_fused.cpp.v2_dataflow.bak): `minirocket_fused_ingest`
 *      drains `input_timeseries` into the internal `raw_samples` stream and
 *      NEVER touches the compute chain or `output_predictions`, so it can
 *      never be blocked by a downstream stall or by compute latency.
 *
 *   2. v3's packed single-packet emit (`minirocket_fused.cpp.v3_singleshot.bak`,
 *      FIX 1: hydra_axis.cpp's PACK_PRED idiom) -- REPLACES v2's original
 *      per-class `for` loop of `num_classes` separate single-beat packets
 *      with ONE 512-bit packet holding all `num_classes` float32 logits
 *      packed into `out_data` bit ranges, `keep = (1 << (num_classes*4)) - 1`,
 *      and exactly ONE guarded non-blocking
 *      `if (!output_predictions.full()) output_predictions.write(out_pkt)`
 *      per completed window (see `minirocket_fused_compute_emit` below).
 *      This is the fix that independently stopped the NetLayer-TX wedge in
 *      v3 (single-shot); the theory for v4 is that reducing "10 separate
 *      per-class writes contending with downstream backpressure" down to
 *      "1 write per window" is what lets the on-chip free-run loop actually
 *      work here, where it previously deadlocked (see history below).
 *
 *   3. `#if BUILD == 1 while (true) { ... }` TRUE on-chip free-run, compiled
 *      in via `-DBUILD=1` for synthesis/ip exports only (see make.tcl.in) --
 *      the kernel self-loops in hardware and drains `input_timeseries` at
 *      fabric rate with no host re-trigger and no XRT/loader autorestart
 *      gap between invocations, unlike v3's single-shot-per-ap_start model.
 *
 * HISTORY -- why this was not simply "flip BUILD=1 back on" for v2:
 *
 *   FREE-RUN DEADLOCK (2026-07-05, see debugging.md "fused free-run
 *   deadlock"): confirmed on hardware TWICE -- both the ORIGINAL single
 *   monolithic `while(true)` FSM (unguarded blocking `output_predictions.write()`,
 *   10 separate per-class packets) AND the v2 DATAFLOW producer/consumer
 *   split with a GUARDED non-blocking write but STILL 10 separate per-class
 *   packets -- the output counter (`app_out`) froze at exactly 22 (~2
 *   windows x 10 classes for InsectSound), permanently. Identical freeze
 *   point under two structurally different fixes ruled OUT the compute-loop/
 *   DATAFLOW structure as the sole cause and implicated the multi-packet
 *   per-window emit pattern itself (matches the independently-observed
 *   hydra_axis.cpp NetLayer udp_out stall on 10-separate-packet emission).
 *   Isolated HLS cosim (bounded free-run repro, COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS=4) passed
 *   clean in both of those cases -- expected, since it can't model
 *   NetLayer/CMAC and therefore never exercises the real downstream
 *   interaction that actually wedges; the same limitation applies to this
 *   v4's bounded-cosim check below (it validates liveness/correctness of
 *   the free-run RTL control flow, NOT real NetLayer/CMAC backpressure
 *   behavior -- that remains a hardware-only risk, see report).
 *
 *   v3 (single-shot, packed emit, BUILT WITHOUT -DBUILD=1) was then proven
 *   on hardware to sustain continuous TX, but XRT/loader ap_start
 *   autorestart between invocations caps host-driven drain at ~35-40k pps
 *   before CMAC backpressures and wedges -- the motivation for this v4
 *   attempt: keep v3's packed emit (which fixed the wedge) but restore v2's
 *   DATAFLOW decouple AND the TRUE on-chip free-run loop, so the kernel
 *   drains the input stream at fabric rate instead of host-spin rate.
 *
 * Two `#pragma HLS DATAFLOW` processes connected by exactly one internal
 * `hls::stream<data_t> raw_samples` channel (canonical single-producer/
 * single-consumer DATAFLOW form, no arrays shared between the two
 * processes):
 *   - `minirocket_fused_ingest`: packet -> float -> `raw_samples` only.
 *     Never touches the compute chain or `output_predictions`, so it can
 *     never be blocked by a downstream stall.
 *   - `minirocket_fused_compute_emit`: buffers `raw_samples` into a window,
 *     runs the compute chain once per full window, and writes ONE packed
 *     prediction packet with a GUARDED, non-blocking
 *     `if (!output_predictions.full()) write()` (drop-on-full, same idiom
 *     as pktDropper.cpp) so it can never block forever either.
 * Together this makes packet ingestion structurally independent of
 * compute/emit, while the guarded write means the process can always make
 * forward progress and the packed single-write means there is only ONE
 * emit-side handshake per window (not `num_classes`) for downstream
 * backpressure to ever catch mid-window.
 * `raw_samples` is sized (`depth=MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH`) to hold a full
 * window -- this doubles as the "producer races ahead while consumer
 * computes" buffering the task asked for (an explicit ping-pong
 * `local_ts0..4` double-buffer was considered but not implemented: the
 * ingest process is already fully decoupled and non-blocking, and the
 * full-window-deep `raw_samples` FIFO already lets it buffer an entire next
 * window's worth of samples while `minirocket_fused_compute_emit` is busy
 * computing on the current window, without ingest ever stalling -- adding a
 * second BRAM-resident ping-pong buffer would double `local_ts0..4` BRAM
 * usage for no additional decoupling this design does not already have, so
 * a single buffer inside `minirocket_fused_compute_emit` is kept, per the
 * task's "single buffer is acceptable for a first free-run test" fallback).
 * External interface (top name, arg order, AXIS ports) is unchanged -- this
 * is purely an internal restructuring.
 *
 * OPERATING MODEL DIFFERENCE FROM minirocket_dpr:
 *   minirocket_dpr shifts a sliding window and re-classifies on EVERY packet
 *   (DP-Reuse only recomputes convolution boundary dot-products, so it's
 *   cheap to do every sample). The Fused core has no incremental algorithm:
 *   every classification requires a full conv+PPV pass over the whole time
 *   series. So this wrapper counts incoming samples into a buffer and only
 *   classifies once, when the `time_series_length`-th sample of a series has
 *   arrived, then resets and starts buffering the next series. One UDP
 *   packet == one sample; ONE packed prediction packet (all num_classes
 *   float32 logits in one 512-bit beat, see v4 FIX 1 above) is emitted once
 *   per full series, not once per packet.
 *
 * MODEL-PARAMETER RELOAD DEVIATION (documented, see report):
 *   minirocket_dpr reloads all model parameters (coefficients/biases/scaler/
 *   dilations) from HBM on EVERY packet, which is affordable there because
 *   every packet also triggers a full classify. Here, most packets are just
 *   buffer writes; reloading ~1024-deep model arrays from HBM on every one of
 *   up to 8192 packets per series would dominate latency (~8192 x ~1000
 *   cycles just for reload, before any compute). So the big parameter arrays
 *   (coefficients/biases/scaler_mean/scaler_scale/dilations/nfpd) are cached
 *   in `static` BRAM and loaded exactly once, guarded by `params_loaded`.
 *   Per the CLAUDE.md "static + ARRAY_PARTITION" gotcha (register inference
 *   fails / II>1), this guard is only applied to arrays that are NOT
 *   `type=complete` partitioned (block/cyclic BRAM partitioning is fine with
 *   static). `local_intercept` is small (<=16 elements) and IS complete-
 *   partitioned, so it is deliberately kept non-static and reloaded every
 *   call instead (cheap, avoids the gotcha entirely).
 */

#include "../include/minirocket_fused.hpp"
#include <cstring>

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fused CONV+PPV weights: plain {-1,+2} float multiply pattern (NOT the
// bFP XNOR/exponent trick minirocket_dpr uses) — matches
// minirocket_modular/_recovered_src_b2b4089/feature_extraction/src/feature_extraction_v16_fixed.cpp
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
static data_t weights[NUM_KERNELS][KERNEL_SIZE] = {
    #include "../include/weights.txt"
};

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fused CONV+PPV feature extraction (full re-compute every call).
// Ported verbatim (loop structure + pragmas) from
// feature_extraction_v16_fixed.cpp's minirocket_feature_extraction_hls(),
// operating on 5 duplicate copies of the time series for conflict-free
// 9-tap sliding-window reads (2 read ports/BRAM x 5 BRAMs = 10 >= 9 needed).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
void minirocket_feature_extraction_hls(
    data_t ts0[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH],
    data_t ts1[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH],
    data_t ts2[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH],
    data_t ts3[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH],
    data_t ts4[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH],
    data_t features[MAX_FEATURES],
    int_t dilations[MAX_DILATIONS],
    int_t num_features_per_dilation[MAX_DILATIONS],
    data_t biases[MAX_FEATURES],
    int_t time_series_length,
    int_t num_dilations,
    int_t num_features
) {
    #pragma HLS INLINE off

    #pragma HLS BIND_STORAGE variable=weights type=rom_1p impl=bram
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=weights complete dim=2
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=weights cyclic factor=28 dim=1

    int_t feature_idx = 0;

    DILATION_LOOP: for (int_t dil_idx = 0; dil_idx < num_dilations; dil_idx++) {
        #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=1 max=16

        int_t dilation = dilations[dil_idx];
        int_t features_this_dilation = num_features_per_dilation[dil_idx];
        int_t _padding0 = dil_idx % 2;
        int_t padding = ((9 - 1) * dilation) / 2;

        KERNEL_GROUP_LOOP: for (int_t kg = 0; kg < NUM_KERNELS; kg += UNROLL_FACTOR) {
            #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=3 max=3

            data_t group_biases[UNROLL_FACTOR][MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION];
            #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=group_biases complete dim=0
            int_t ppv_counts[UNROLL_FACTOR][MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION];
            #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=ppv_counts complete dim=0
            int_t padding_flag[UNROLL_FACTOR];
            #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=padding_flag complete

            LOAD_BIASES: for (int_t bi = 0; bi < UNROLL_FACTOR * MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION; bi++) {
                #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=84 max=84
                int_t ki = bi / MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION;
                int_t f = bi % MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION;
                int_t kernel_idx = kg + ki;
                int_t base = feature_idx + kernel_idx * features_this_dilation;
                group_biases[ki][f] = (f < features_this_dilation && kernel_idx < NUM_KERNELS && base + f < num_features)
                                      ? biases[base + f] : (data_t)0.0;
                ppv_counts[ki][f] = 0;
                if (f == 0) {
                    padding_flag[ki] = (_padding0 + kernel_idx) % 2;
                }
            }

            CONV_LOOP: for (int_t j = 0; j < time_series_length; j++) {
                #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=150 max=8192

                data_t sw[KERNEL_SIZE];
                #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=sw complete

                int_t idx0 = j + (-4) * dilation;
                int_t idx1 = j + (-3) * dilation;
                int_t idx2 = j + (-2) * dilation;
                int_t idx3 = j + (-1) * dilation;
                int_t idx4 = j;
                int_t idx5 = j + (1) * dilation;
                int_t idx6 = j + (2) * dilation;
                int_t idx7 = j + (3) * dilation;
                int_t idx8 = j + (4) * dilation;

                sw[0] = (idx0 < 0 || idx0 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts0[idx0];
                sw[1] = (idx1 < 0 || idx1 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts0[idx1];
                sw[2] = (idx2 < 0 || idx2 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts1[idx2];
                sw[3] = (idx3 < 0 || idx3 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts1[idx3];
                sw[4] = (idx4 < 0 || idx4 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts2[idx4];
                sw[5] = (idx5 < 0 || idx5 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts2[idx5];
                sw[6] = (idx6 < 0 || idx6 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts3[idx6];
                sw[7] = (idx7 < 0 || idx7 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts3[idx7];
                sw[8] = (idx8 < 0 || idx8 >= time_series_length) ? (data_t)0.0 : ts4[idx8];

                bool in_padded_range = (j >= padding && j < time_series_length - padding);

                PARALLEL_KERNELS: for (int_t ki = 0; ki < UNROLL_FACTOR; ki++) {
                    #pragma HLS UNROLL
                    data_t value = 0.0;
                    DOT_PRODUCT: for (int_t k = 0; k < KERNEL_SIZE; k++) {
                        #pragma HLS UNROLL
                        value += sw[k] * weights[kg + ki][k];
                    }

                    bool use_position = (padding_flag[ki] == 0) || in_padded_range;
                    PPV_FEATURES: for (int_t f = 0; f < MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION; f++) {
                        #pragma HLS UNROLL
                        if (f < features_this_dilation && use_position && value > group_biases[ki][f]) {
                            ppv_counts[ki][f]++;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            int_t padded_len = time_series_length - (int_t)(2 * padding);
            data_t inv_denom_full = (data_t)1.0 / (data_t)time_series_length;
            data_t inv_denom_padded = (padded_len > 0) ? (data_t)1.0 / (data_t)padded_len : (data_t)0.0;

            WRITE_PPV: for (int_t wi = 0; wi < UNROLL_FACTOR * MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION; wi++) {
                #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=28 max=84
                int_t ki = wi / MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION;
                int_t f = wi % MAX_FEATURES_PER_DILATION;
                int_t kernel_idx = kg + ki;
                if (kernel_idx < NUM_KERNELS && f < features_this_dilation) {
                    int_t base = feature_idx + kernel_idx * features_this_dilation;
                    if (base + f < num_features) {
                        data_t inv_denom = (padding_flag[ki] == 0) ? inv_denom_full : inv_denom_padded;
                        features[base + f] = (data_t)ppv_counts[ki][f] * inv_denom;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        feature_idx += features_this_dilation * NUM_KERNELS;
    }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Z-normalization scaler. Ported from minirocket_dpr's apply_scaler_hls
// (divide by scaler_scale directly), NOT scaler.cpp's multiply-by-inv_scale
// form, because this top's interface (matching minirocket_dpr) is handed
// scaler_scale, not a precomputed reciprocal. Mathematically identical to
// Python's sklearn StandardScaler.transform().
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
void apply_scaler_hls(
    data_t features[MAX_FEATURES],
    data_t scaled_features[MAX_FEATURES],
    data_t scaler_mean[MAX_FEATURES],
    data_t scaler_scale[MAX_FEATURES],
    int_t num_features
) {
    #pragma HLS INLINE off
    SCALE_LOOP: for (int_t i = 0; i < num_features; i++) {
        #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
        #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=100 max=1024
        scaled_features[i] = (features[i] - scaler_mean[i]) / scaler_scale[i];
    }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Ridge classifier. Ported from classifier.cpp's linear_classifier_predict_hls,
// with the FEATURE_LOOP bound changed from MAX_FEATURES+conditional to the
// runtime num_features (matches the variable-bound + LOOP_TRIPCOUNT idiom
// already used throughout minirocket_dpr; avoids MAX_FEATURES-1024 wasted
// cycles per class when num_features < 1024, e.g. 840 for all 3 datasets
// evaluated here). Binary-flip special case (lines 29-33 of classifier.cpp)
// kept verbatim: only coefficients[0]/intercept[0] are meaningful for
// num_classes==2, the loader zero-fills row 1.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
void linear_classifier_predict_hls(
    data_t scaled_features[MAX_FEATURES],
    data_t predictions[MAX_CLASSES],
    data_t coefficients[MAX_CLASSES][MAX_FEATURES],
    data_t intercept[MAX_CLASSES],
    int_t num_features,
    int_t num_classes
) {
    #pragma HLS INLINE off

    // v5 (2026-07-11): accumulate in facc_t (ap_fixed<48,24>) instead of
    // float. The float multiply keeps full precision and pipelines freely
    // (no loop-carried dependency); only the ADD is on the carried path,
    // and a 48-bit fixed add is 1 cycle => FEATURE_LOOP true II=1 (was
    // II=4 with the float accumulator — see include/minirocket_fused.hpp).
    if (num_classes == 2) {
        facc_t score = (facc_t)intercept[0];
        BINARY_FEATURE_LOOP: for (int_t j = 0; j < num_features; j++) {
            #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=100 max=1024
            score += (facc_t)(coefficients[0][j] * scaled_features[j]);
        }
        predictions[0] = (data_t)0.0 - (data_t)score;
        predictions[1] = (data_t)score;
    } else {
        CLASS_LOOP: for (int_t i = 0; i < num_classes; i++) {
            #pragma HLS PIPELINE off
            #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=2 max=16
            facc_t score = (facc_t)intercept[i];
            FEATURE_LOOP: for (int_t j = 0; j < num_features; j++) {
                #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                #pragma HLS LOOP_TRIPCOUNT min=100 max=1024
                score += (facc_t)(coefficients[i][j] * scaled_features[j]);
            }
            predictions[i] = (data_t)score;
        }
    }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DATAFLOW producer: packet -> float -> `raw_samples` ONLY. Never touches
// the compute chain or `output_predictions`, so nothing downstream can ever
// block this process -- packet ingestion is now structurally independent of
// compute/emit (see file header "HISTORY"). Non-blocking: only acts when a
// packet is actually available.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
void minirocket_fused_ingest(
    hls::stream<pkt> &input_timeseries,
    hls::stream<data_t> &raw_samples,
    int_t time_series_length
) {
    #pragma HLS INLINE off

#if defined(COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS)
    // TEST-ONLY bounded free-run loop -- see file header and
    // minirocket_fused_compute_emit's identical guard below. Never active
    // for synthesis/ip/hw builds.
    for (int __it = 0; __it < (COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS) * (int)time_series_length + 64; __it++) {
#elif BUILD == 1
    while (true) {
#endif
        if (!input_timeseries.empty()) {
            // ALWAYS drain the NetLayer app-in stream when a packet is
            // available -- this read must never depend on raw_samples state,
            // or the AXI-stream handshake with NetLayer stalls and the whole
            // RX path wedges (observed >~2.24M pps FPGA-to-FPGA).
            pkt v = input_timeseries.read();
            ap_uint< DWIDTH > tmp = v.data;
            data_t new_val = *((data_t*) &tmp);
            // DROP-ON-FULL: forward to the compute FIFO only if there is room;
            // otherwise discard this sample rather than block the read above.
            // Same guarded idiom as output_predictions (below) / pktDropper.cpp.
            // Converts the high-rate wedge into a graceful saturation knee:
            // throughput plateaus at the compute ceiling, loss rises smoothly.
            if (!raw_samples.full()) {
                raw_samples.write(new_val);
            }
        }
#if defined(COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS) || BUILD == 1
    }
#endif
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DATAFLOW consumer: buffers `raw_samples` into a window (5 duplicate
// copies, conflict-free 9-tap reads, same as before), runs the fused
// compute chain once per full window, and emits ONE packed prediction
// packet (v4 FIX 1, see file header) with a GUARDED, non-blocking write --
// `if (!output_predictions.full())` -- mirroring pktDropper.cpp's
// `if (!output.full()) write()` idiom instead of the original unguarded
// blocking write. This process can therefore never stall forever waiting
// on a downstream consumer, which is what fixes the hardware free-run
// deadlock (see file header "HISTORY").
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
void minirocket_fused_compute_emit(
    hls::stream<data_t> &raw_samples,
    hls::stream<pkt> &output_predictions,
    data_t* coefficients,
    data_t* intercept,
    data_t* scaler_mean,
    data_t* scaler_scale,
    int_t* dilations,
    int_t* num_features_per_dilation,
    data_t* biases,
    int_t time_series_length,
    int_t num_features,
    int_t num_classes,
    int_t num_dilations
) {
    #pragma HLS INLINE off

    // 5 duplicate copies of the buffered series (conflict-free 9-tap reads),
    // persisted across per-packet calls -- this IS the buffer. No
    // ARRAY_PARTITION applied (bandwidth comes from the 5x duplication, not
    // partitioning), so `static` here does not trip the "static +
    // ARRAY_PARTITION" gotcha.
    static data_t local_ts0[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH];
    static data_t local_ts1[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH];
    static data_t local_ts2[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH];
    static data_t local_ts3[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH];
    static data_t local_ts4[MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH];
    static int_t sample_count = 0;

    // Model parameters: cached once (see file header comment on the reload
    // deviation from minirocket_dpr). Only block/cyclic (BRAM) partitioned
    // arrays are made static; the complete-partitioned intercept is not.
    static bool params_loaded = false;
    static data_t local_coefficients[MAX_CLASSES][MAX_FEATURES];
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=local_coefficients type=block factor=4 dim=1
    static data_t local_scaler_mean[MAX_FEATURES];
    static data_t local_scaler_scale[MAX_FEATURES];
    static data_t local_biases[MAX_FEATURES];
    static int_t local_dilations[MAX_DILATIONS];
    static int_t local_num_features_per_dilation[MAX_DILATIONS];

    data_t local_intercept[MAX_CLASSES];
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=local_intercept type=complete

    // Transient per-series scratch (not persisted, no need to be static).
    data_t local_features[MAX_FEATURES];
    data_t local_scaled_features[MAX_FEATURES];
    data_t local_predictions[MAX_CLASSES];
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=local_features type=cyclic factor=8
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=local_scaled_features type=cyclic factor=8

    // One-time copy of the bulk model parameters from global memory.
    if (!params_loaded) {
        COPY_DILATIONS: for (int_t i = 0; i < num_dilations; i++) {
            #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            local_dilations[i] = dilations[i];
            local_num_features_per_dilation[i] = num_features_per_dilation[i];
        }

        COPY_BIASES: for (int_t i = 0; i < num_features; i++) {
            #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            local_biases[i] = biases[i];
            local_scaler_mean[i] = scaler_mean[i];
            local_scaler_scale[i] = scaler_scale[i];
        }

        COPY_COEF: for (int_t i = 0; i < num_classes; i++) {
            for (int_t j = 0; j < num_features; j++) {
                #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                local_coefficients[i][j] = coefficients[i * num_features + j];
            }
        }

        params_loaded = true;
    }

#if defined(COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS)
    // TEST-ONLY bounded free-run loop -- see file header and
    // minirocket_fused_ingest's identical guard above. Never active for
    // synthesis/ip/hw builds.
    for (int __it = 0; __it < (COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS) * (int)time_series_length + 64; __it++) {
#elif BUILD == 1
    while (true) {
#endif
        if (!raw_samples.empty()) {
            data_t new_val = raw_samples.read();

            // Ingest one sample into the buffer-so-far (5 duplicate copies).
            if (sample_count >= 0 && sample_count < time_series_length &&
                sample_count < MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH) {
                local_ts0[sample_count] = new_val;
                local_ts1[sample_count] = new_val;
                local_ts2[sample_count] = new_val;
                local_ts3[sample_count] = new_val;
                local_ts4[sample_count] = new_val;
                sample_count++;
            }

            // Full series buffered -> run ONE fused compute + emit once.
            if (time_series_length > 0 && sample_count == time_series_length) {

                // Intercept is small (<=16 elements): cheap enough to reload
                // every window unconditionally rather than risk
                // static+complete-partition register inference issues.
                COPY_INTERCEPT: for (int_t i = 0; i < num_classes; i++) {
                    #pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    local_intercept[i] = intercept[i];
                }

                minirocket_feature_extraction_hls(
                    local_ts0, local_ts1, local_ts2, local_ts3, local_ts4,
                    local_features,
                    local_dilations,
                    local_num_features_per_dilation,
                    local_biases,
                    time_series_length,
                    num_dilations,
                    num_features
                );

                apply_scaler_hls(
                    local_features, local_scaled_features,
                    local_scaler_mean, local_scaler_scale, num_features
                );

                linear_classifier_predict_hls(
                    local_scaled_features, local_predictions,
                    local_coefficients, local_intercept,
                    num_features, num_classes
                );

                // v4 FIX 1 -- packed single-packet emit (mirrors
                // hydra_axis.cpp PACK_PRED and v3's
                // minirocket_fused.cpp.v3_singleshot.bak, ~lines 455-479):
                // pack all num_classes float32 logits into the low
                // num_classes*4 bytes of ONE 512-bit packet instead of
                // num_classes separate single-beat packets, then ONE
                // GUARDED, non-blocking write (fix for candidate (a)): if
                // downstream (NetLayer TX) is backpressuring, drop this
                // whole prediction packet instead of blocking forever --
                // same idiom as pktDropper.cpp's `if (!output.full())
                // write()`. Bug-B sideband kept (dest=0/user=0/id=0/strb=-1).
                {
                    pkt out_pkt;
                    ap_uint<DWIDTH> out_data = 0;
                    PACK_PRED: for (int_t c = 0; c < MAX_CLASSES; c++) {
                        #pragma HLS UNROLL
                        if (c < num_classes) {
                            ap_uint<32> bits = *((ap_uint<32>*)&local_predictions[c]);
                            out_data.range(32 * c + 31, 32 * c) = bits;
                        }
                    }
                    out_pkt.data = out_data;
                    // Mark only the num_classes*4 payload bytes as valid; rest zero.
                    out_pkt.keep = (ap_uint<DWIDTH/8>(1) << (num_classes * 4)) - 1;
                    out_pkt.strb = -1;
                    out_pkt.last = 1;
                    out_pkt.dest = 0;
                    out_pkt.user = 0;
                    out_pkt.id   = 0;
                    if (!output_predictions.full()) {
                        output_predictions.write(out_pkt);
                    }
                    // else: downstream is backpressuring -- drop this
                    // prediction packet rather than stall the compute
                    // process (and, by extension via the raw_samples
                    // handshake, ingestion) forever.
                }

                // Reset for the next series.
                sample_count = 0;
            }
        }
#if defined(COSIM_MAX_WINDOWS) || BUILD == 1
    }
#endif
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Top-level network AXIS kernel: buffer-then-classify, v4 (DATAFLOW split +
// packed emit + TRUE on-chip free-run, see file header). The ingest and
// compute/emit processes below communicate through exactly one internal
// `hls::stream<data_t> raw_samples` channel (canonical single-producer/
// single-consumer DATAFLOW form -- no arrays are shared between the two
// processes). External interface (top name, arg order, AXIS ports)
// unchanged from v2/v3.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
extern "C" void minirocket_fused_inference(
    hls::stream<pkt> &input_timeseries,
    hls::stream<pkt> &output_predictions,
    data_t* coefficients,
    data_t* intercept,
    data_t* scaler_mean,
    data_t* scaler_scale,
    int_t* dilations,
    int_t* num_features_per_dilation,
    data_t* biases,
    int_t time_series_length,
    int_t num_features,
    int_t num_classes,
    int_t num_dilations
) {

    #pragma HLS INTERFACE axis port = input_timeseries
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE axis port = output_predictions
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=coefficients bundle=gmem2 depth=16384
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=intercept bundle=gmem3 depth=16
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=scaler_mean bundle=gmem4 depth=1024
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=scaler_scale bundle=gmem5 depth=1024
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=dilations bundle=gmem6 depth=16
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=num_features_per_dilation bundle=gmem7 depth=16
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=biases bundle=gmem8 depth=1024

    #pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=time_series_length bundle=control
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=num_features bundle=control
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=num_classes bundle=control
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=num_dilations bundle=control
    #pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=return bundle=control

    #pragma HLS DATAFLOW

    // Internal ingest -> compute/emit channel. Depth = a full window so
    // normal one-window producer/consumer skew never blocks ingest either
    // (the guarded emit write above is what bounds compute/emit itself).
    hls::stream<data_t> raw_samples("raw_samples");
    #pragma HLS STREAM variable=raw_samples depth=MAX_TIME_SERIES_LENGTH

    minirocket_fused_ingest(input_timeseries, raw_samples, time_series_length);

    minirocket_fused_compute_emit(
        raw_samples, output_predictions,
        coefficients, intercept, scaler_mean, scaler_scale,
        dilations, num_features_per_dilation, biases,
        time_series_length, num_features, num_classes, num_dilations
    );
}
